# These FIGfont files are byte-exact test fixtures, not source code.
#
# Both runners read them and their rendered output is compared byte-for-byte, and
# several are deliberately CRLF-terminated to prove the parsers agree on \r\n
# handling. Git's eol normalisation would rewrite those to LF on commit and
# checkout, silently deleting the CRLF cases and making the score differ between
# a fresh clone and this working tree. -text turns all of it off.
*.flf -text
